  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25146468",
      "title": "Adding the \"Change Password\" Logic",
      "lectureOrder": 411,
      "videoOrder": 379,
      "sourceHash": "5a8b6e1c2e3627122cababcb4b3f3bdf68a2ee668885300879624350add66c32",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.17,
          "end": 3.56,
          "en": "Okay, so now that we've got",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.56,
          "end": 6.48,
          "en": "this protection code here in place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.48,
          "end": 9.04,
          "en": "in the next step, we know that this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.04,
          "end": 11.27,
          "en": "is coming from an authenticated user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.27,
          "end": 15.57,
          "en": "and we know that it's a request with the right method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.57,
          "end": 17.64,
          "en": "So now we need to extract data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.64,
          "end": 21.1,
          "en": "from the incoming request, the old and the new password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.1,
          "end": 25.91,
          "en": "and we will also need the email address of that user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.91,
          "end": 27.95,
          "en": "because of course, in the database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.95,
          "end": 30.6,
          "en": "we store users with emails and passwords",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.6,
          "end": 33.14,
          "en": "and if we wanna change the password of a user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.14,
          "end": 35.92,
          "en": "we need that email address of the user as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.92,
          "end": 38.47,
          "en": "to identify that user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.47,
          "end": 41.94,
          "en": "Thankfully, getting that email address is not too difficult",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.94,
          "end": 44.39,
          "en": "even though it's not part of this form here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.39,
          "end": 49.24,
          "en": "because we do encode the email address in our token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.24,
          "end": 53.87,
          "en": "We return that object here in our nextauth file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.87,
          "end": 56.19,
          "en": "and that data ends up in the token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.19,
          "end": 59.283,
          "en": "and therefore, it's part of that session, which we get here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.27,
          "end": 62.77,
          "en": "So we can get the userEmail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.77,
          "end": 67.77,
          "en": "by accessing session.user.email here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.39,
          "end": 71.68,
          "en": "and we can then also get the other data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.68,
          "end": 75.33,
          "en": "like the oldPassword by reaching out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.33,
          "end": 76.9,
          "en": "to the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.9,
          "end": 79.82,
          "en": "and there the body field as we learned it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.82,
          "end": 82.31,
          "en": "So that's what we also do in the signup.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.31,
          "end": 83.76,
          "en": "when we create a user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.76,
          "end": 87.07,
          "en": "There we also get the email and password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.07,
          "end": 89.803,
          "en": "by diving into the request.body in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.87,
          "end": 92.91,
          "en": "And here in change-password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.91,
          "end": 96.11,
          "en": "we could, for example, expect that on the body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.11,
          "end": 99.81,
          "en": "we got a oldPassword field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.81,
          "end": 102.12,
          "en": "and then we got the newPassword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.12,
          "end": 104.27000000000001,
          "en": "which we get from request.body.newPassword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.81,
          "end": 107.55,
          "en": "Of course, we'll have to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.55,
          "end": 109.86,
          "en": "that when we send the request from the client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.86,
          "end": 111.25,
          "en": "to the server later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.25,
          "end": 114.08,
          "en": "that we have old and newPassword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.08,
          "end": 117.86,
          "en": "that we have these two fields in the request data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.86,
          "end": 120.193,
          "en": "which we attach to the outgoing request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.16,
          "end": 123.82,
          "en": "And with that, we've got all the data we need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.82,
          "end": 126.03,
          "en": "Now we wanna connect to the database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.03,
          "end": 128.68,
          "en": "and find a user by that email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.68,
          "end": 130.39,
          "en": "and then once we got that user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.39,
          "end": 133.22,
          "en": "we wanna check if the oldPassword is correct,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.22,
          "end": 136.04,
          "en": "so if it matches the password currently stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.04,
          "end": 137.26,
          "en": "in the database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 137.26,
          "end": 138.72,
          "en": "and if that's then the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 138.72,
          "end": 141.19,
          "en": "we wanna hash the newPassword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.19,
          "end": 145.043,
          "en": "and replace the oldPassword with the new one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 146.18,
          "end": 151.15,
          "en": "And for this, of course, we can call connectToDatabase again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 151.15,
          "end": 155.563,
          "en": "and import that from our lib/db file like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.35,
          "end": 159.75,
          "en": "And then here call connectToDatabase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.75,
          "end": 161.79,
          "en": "and await this, of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.79,
          "end": 164.28,
          "en": "and here we then get the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.28,
          "end": 166.28,
          "en": "And then once we got the client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 166.28,
          "end": 168.53,
          "en": "we can reach out to the database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 168.53,
          "end": 170.85,
          "en": "and then there to the collection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 170.85,
          "end": 174.853,
          "en": "that stores our users, which is the users collection here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 176.97,
          "end": 180.889,
          "en": "So here we then reach out to the users collection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.889,
          "end": 181.722,
          "en": "usersCollection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 181.722,
          "end": 185.92,
          "en": "I can store access to that collection in a separate constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.92,
          "end": 190.03,
          "en": "and then we can use that usersCollection to findOne user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.03,
          "end": 193.01,
          "en": "by email as we did it before as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.01,
          "end": 195.77,
          "en": "in the authentication code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.77,
          "end": 198.197,
          "en": "There we also find a user by email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.197,
          "end": 200.78,
          "en": "and now we're going to do the same thing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 200.78,
          "end": 203.43,
          "en": "We look for the email field in our documents",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.43,
          "end": 205.71,
          "en": "and check if we find one document",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 205.71,
          "end": 208.62,
          "en": "where the email address stored in the document",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 208.62,
          "end": 211.603,
          "en": "is equal to the userEmail we get from the session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 212.6,
          "end": 214.93,
          "en": "Now, this will return a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.93,
          "end": 219.22,
          "en": "so we await that and then we'll get a user document",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 219.22,
          "end": 222.51,
          "en": "or not but if we somehow don't find a user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 222.51,
          "end": 224.18,
          "en": "something is wrong anyways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 224.18,
          "end": 227.47,
          "en": "because that userEmail is coming from the session,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 227.47,
          "end": 230.45,
          "en": "so it would be strange if we have a logged in user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 230.45,
          "end": 234.52,
          "en": "and yet he or she is missing from the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 234.52,
          "end": 237.123,
          "en": "But still, we can also handle that case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 238.21,
          "end": 240.14,
          "en": "Close our connection here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 240.14,
          "end": 243.19,
          "en": "and then possibly also return some error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 243.19,
          "end": 245.37,
          "en": "This could be a 404 error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 245.37,
          "end": 250.37,
          "en": "where we say user not found or something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 252.36,
          "end": 254.24,
          "en": "Now, if we make it past this check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 254.24,
          "end": 255.83,
          "en": "which we typically should,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 255.83,
          "end": 258.21,
          "en": "we can now verify the password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 258.21,
          "end": 260.18,
          "en": "So we get the currentPassword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 260.18,
          "end": 262.91,
          "en": "by accessing user.password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 262.91,
          "end": 266.07,
          "en": "So this user document, which we get from the database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 266.07,
          "end": 267.86,
          "en": "and there, the password field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 267.86,
          "end": 269.933,
          "en": "which is this hashed password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 271.02,
          "end": 272.92,
          "en": "That's the currentPassword now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 272.92,
          "end": 274.77,
          "en": "and now we wanna verify this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 274.77,
          "end": 277.3,
          "en": "and for that, in the lib folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 277.3,
          "end": 282.3,
          "en": "we have this auth.js file with the verifyPassword function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 282.57,
          "end": 284.69,
          "en": "And I wanna call this function now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 286.18,
          "end": 291.18,
          "en": "and hence, we need to import verifyPassword from lib/auth.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 291.28,
          "end": 293.32,
          "en": "We need to add this import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 294.72,
          "end": 298.59000000000003,
          "en": "and with it imported, we can call verifyPassword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 298.59000000000003,
          "end": 302.49,
          "en": "and pass in the incoming password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 302.49,
          "end": 305.62,
          "en": "so the oldPassword in our case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 305.62,
          "end": 307.76,
          "en": "as a first argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 307.76,
          "end": 310.44,
          "en": "and then the stored hashed password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 310.44,
          "end": 312.08,
          "en": "to which we wanna compare it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 312.08,
          "end": 316.423,
          "en": "So this currentPassword here as a second argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 317.71,
          "end": 319.13,
          "en": "And we then await this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 319.13,
          "end": 321.42,
          "en": "because that returns a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 321.42,
          "end": 324.73,
          "en": "and we get back the answer to the question",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 324.73,
          "end": 328.03,
          "en": "whether the passwords are equal or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 328.03,
          "end": 330.63,
          "en": "And if they are not equal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 330.63,
          "end": 332.373,
          "en": "if not passwordsAreEqual,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 333.84000000000003,
          "end": 336.18,
          "en": "if that is false, then we know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 336.18,
          "end": 340.69,
          "en": "that the old password entered here simply does not match",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 340.69,
          "end": 342.36,
          "en": "the user's password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 342.36,
          "end": 345.04,
          "en": "And in this case, we don't wanna allow the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 345.04,
          "end": 347.62,
          "en": "to change the password, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 347.62,
          "end": 349.42,
          "en": "So here we wanna return.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 349.42,
          "end": 354.063,
          "en": "We wanna also close our client connection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 355.15,
          "end": 357.89,
          "en": "And we wanna send back a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 357.89,
          "end": 361.46,
          "en": "where the status code could be 403,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 361.46,
          "end": 365.98,
          "en": "not 401 as it was before but 403",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 365.98,
          "end": 368.8,
          "en": "where we say you are authenticated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 368.8,
          "end": 371.3,
          "en": "that's why it's not 401,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 371.3,
          "end": 374.743,
          "en": "but you're not authorized for this operation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 374.743,
          "end": 377.48,
          "en": "You simply do not have the permissions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 377.48,
          "end": 379.46,
          "en": "to perform this operation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 379.46,
          "end": 381.67,
          "en": "even though you're authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 381.67,
          "end": 384.66,
          "en": "And in this case, the user doesn't have the permissions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 384.66,
          "end": 386.82,
          "en": "for this specific operation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 386.82,
          "end": 389.033,
          "en": "because the passwords are not equal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 389.91,
          "end": 393.63,
          "en": "Of course, alternatively, we could also use 422,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 393.63,
          "end": 397.99,
          "en": "which kind of indicates that the user input is incorrect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 397.99,
          "end": 400.78,
          "en": "And that would be a fair assumption here as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 400.78,
          "end": 404.49,
          "en": "that the user simply mistyped the old password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 404.49,
          "end": 407.82,
